  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kuru-ko Wate Commercial Vegetables Capacity Building Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Irrigated agriculture (jute, kale, cabbage, tomato, okra, pepper, amaranthus, pumpkin, watermelon, pig weed) , Town/City: Juba Nabari, South Sudan, Summary: The purpose of this grant is to expand Kuru-ko Wate Self Help&apos;s operations as a sustainable farming cooperative and ensure food security and increased income for its members. KKWSH will purchase vegetables from members and process them for resale in commercial markets. Activities will include laying a drip irrigation network to ensure a steady supply of water, procuring farming equipment and inputs as well as two rickshaws for transporting vegetables. Funds will also be used to sponsor financial management, monitoring and evaluation, business management and agronomy training in order to strengthen the capacity of the group.</narrative>
  </description>
